00:41:03,157 --> 00:41:09,157
Stuck in the Suburbs is a 2004 American comedy film that
premiered as a Disney Channel Original Movie.

11
00:45:09,473 --> 00:45:15,473
It was released on July 16, 2004, and stars Danielle Panabaker as
Brittany Aarons and Brenda Song as Natasha Kwon-Schwartz.

12
00:49:15,789 --> 00:49:21,789
Brittany, a regular middle school student in the suburbs, accidentally
exchanges cell phones with pop singer Jordan Cahill.

13
00:53:22,105 --> 00:53:28,105
This was one of the first television films by Disney to
be accompanied by its own soundtrack.

14
00:57:28,421 --> 00:57:34,421
The film gathered 3.7 million viewers which made the film the most-watched
telecast in its time period in the kids 6–11 and 9–14 demographics.

15
01:01:34,736 --> 01:01:40,736
The film's soundtrack entered the U.S.

16
01:05:41,052 --> 01:05:47,052
Billboard 200 and peaked at #5 on the Billboard Top Kid Audio charts.

17
01:09:47,368 --> 01:09:53,368
The film explores themes of pop star, female friendship,
teen movie, cell phone, best friends.

18
01:13:53,684 --> 01:13:59,684
The tone is lighthearted.
